# Copy to .env.stack.local or pass these values through your shell.
# Do not commit .env.stack.local or any working secret values.
#
# Hard-cut rename: former .env.p10.local is not read. Recreate from this example.
# Volume rename (stack-postgres-data) starts a fresh local database unless you migrate data manually.
#
# === Primary profile: ingress-wired HTTP Compose (P10-01 / P10-02) ===
# CONTEXT_ENGINE_TESTING=true with the full CE_* quartet enables peer/Origin/CSRF
# while allowing http://127.0.0.1 origins. This is Compose config evidence, not
# deployment evidence / not P12 (true testing=false requires HTTPS).
# Use http://127.0.0.1 (not localhost) so browser Origin matches CE_STACK_PUBLIC_ORIGIN.
# When changing STACK_FRONTEND_PORT, update CE_STACK_PUBLIC_ORIGIN to the same port.
#
# Boot order: postgres → migrate → bootstrap (insert-only admin) → api ready → worker ready → frontend.
# CE_ADMIN_* are consumed only by the Compose bootstrap one-shot (not api/worker).
# Core-path smoke (BFF CSRF→login→SSE; API may inline turns under testing), after stack is up:
#   python app/scripts/stack_smoke_core.py --env-file app/.env.stack.local
# Worker-path smoke (Compose-dev matrix only — not TLS / not P12). Requires inline off:
#   CE_INLINE_TURN_WORKERS=false python app/scripts/stack_smoke_worker.py --env-file app/.env.stack.local
# Operator runbook: docs/operations/compose-stack-runbook.md

POSTGRES_DB=<set locally>
POSTGRES_USER=<set locally>
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<set locally>

# Host-native scripts/dev.sh only. Compose uses the internal postgres service.
# Set these when Postgres is published to the host (for example 127.0.0.1:5438).
POSTGRES_HOST=127.0.0.1
POSTGRES_PORT=5432

CE_ADMIN_USERNAME=<set locally>
CE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=<set locally>

# Local HTTP stack requires the session cookie to be sent over http://127.0.0.1.
CE_SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=false

CONTEXT_ENGINE_TESTING=true

# Shared public origin for FastAPI (CE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN) and BFF (CONTEXT_ENGINE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN).
CE_STACK_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:3000
CE_INTERNAL_HOSTS=api
# Frontend container static IP on compose network ce_stack (see compose.stack.yml).
CE_TRUSTED_BFF_PEERS=172.30.55.10/32
# Dedicated CSRF key: >=32 bytes and must differ from CONFIG_ENCRYPTION_KEY.
CE_CSRF_SIGNING_KEY=local-dev-csrf-signing-key-min-32b!!
# Purpose-derived graph refs (HMAC). Distinct from CSRF/Fernet; rotate invalidates node URL selections.
# Local demo first-run may generate this into the gitignored env file; do not commit real values.
CE_GRAPH_REF_KEY=local-dev-graph-ref-key-min-32-bytes!!
# Optional graph-read admission (zero wait queue):
# CE_GRAPH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=10
# CE_GRAPH_GLOBAL_CONCURRENCY=8
# CE_GRAPH_PER_DOMAIN_CONCURRENCY=2
# CE_GRAPH_PER_PRINCIPAL_CONCURRENCY=2
CE_SESSION_IDLE_TTL_SECONDS=1800
CE_SESSION_TOUCH_INTERVAL_SECONDS=60
CE_LOGIN_THROTTLE_WINDOW_SECONDS=300
CE_LOGIN_THROTTLE_MAX_FAILURES=5
CE_LOGIN_THROTTLE_BLOCK_SECONDS=900

# Fernet key generated locally, for example:
# python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
# Must not equal CE_CSRF_SIGNING_KEY.
CONFIG_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<set locally — distinct from CE_CSRF_SIGNING_KEY>

# Used by host-native scripts/dev.sh. Compose frontend hardcodes http://api:8000.
CONTEXT_ENGINE_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8000

STACK_API_PORT=8000
STACK_FRONTEND_PORT=3000

# Optional: idle sleep between empty worker poll rounds (seconds).
# CE_WORKER_IDLE_SECONDS=2

# --- Worker-path smoke only (Compose-dev matrix; requires CONTEXT_ENGINE_TESTING=true) ---
# Unset → API inlines turn workers when testing=true (P10-02 default).
# Set false so Compose worker claims turns; never treat as production/release config.
# CE_INLINE_TURN_WORKERS=false
# Optional smoke knobs (do not change default compose values permanently):
# CE_WORKER_IDLE_SECONDS=0.2
# CE_TURN_LEASE_SECONDS=10
# CE_TURN_WORKER_ID=compose-turn-worker

# Optional: per-Knowledge Graph soft storage limit shown in Settings storage bars.
# Default is 5 GiB.
# CE_DOMAIN_STORAGE_LIMIT_BYTES=5368709120

# --- Secondary bypass (not the green path; not ingress evidence) ---
# Leave CE_STACK_PUBLIC_ORIGIN, CE_INTERNAL_HOSTS, CE_TRUSTED_BFF_PEERS, and
# CE_CSRF_SIGNING_KEY empty/unset with CONTEXT_ENGINE_TESTING=true to disable
# request-security policy (test bypass). Partial CE_* sets still fail closed.
# Do not treat bypass as production-like or P12 evidence.

# --- Optional TLS ingress overlay (P12-05 evidence lane; not default CI) ---
# Requires generated host certs (never commit key material):
#   python app/scripts/generate_stack_tls_certs.py
# Then set:
#   CE_STACK_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://127.0.0.1:8443
#   CE_SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=true
#   CONTEXT_ENGINE_TESTING=false
#   CE_INLINE_TURN_WORKERS=false
#   CE_STACK_TLS_CERT_DIR=<absolute path to app/.stack-tls>
#   STACK_TLS_PORT=8443
#   CE_STACK_TLS_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Boot:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.stack.local \
#     -f compose.stack.yml -f compose.stack.tls.yml up --build -d
# Trust proof (AE4):
#   python app/scripts/stack_ingress_trust_proof.py --env-file app/.env.stack.local
# SSE proof (AE1/AE2; requires OPENAI_API_KEY in host env-file — never commit):
#   python app/scripts/stack_ingress_sse_proof.py --env-file app/.env.stack.local --domain-id <domainPublicId>
# Drain proof (AE3 stop order / stop_claim):
#   python app/scripts/stack_ingress_drain_proof.py --env-file app/.env.stack.local
#
# CE_STACK_TLS_CERT_DIR=<absolute host path to cert.pem+key.pem dir>
# STACK_TLS_PORT=8443
# CE_STACK_TLS_HOST=127.0.0.1

# --- Host live-test credentials (optional; never commit) ---
# For credential-gated host scripts only (provider staging smoke, TLS/SSE proof).
# Not sealed Settings credentials; Compose api/worker do not consume these keys.
# Unsupported: app/.env — put keys here in .env.stack.local instead.
# Scripts may still accept CE_OPENAI_API_KEY / CE_REDUCTO_API_KEY if already set.
OPENAI_API_KEY=<set locally>
REDUCTO_API_KEY=<set locally>

# --- Optional live Docker LightRAG overlay (P5-04 evidence lane; not default CI) ---
# Pins CE_DOMAIN_RUNTIME_CONTROLLER_KIND=docker + CE_LIGHTRAG_CLIENT_KIND=native
# via compose.stack.live.yml. Default compose.stack.yml stays local/local.
#
# Requires: Docker daemon and a host-absolute path bind-mounted identically into
# api/worker so sibling domain containers see the same runtime dir (Docker bind
# src is host-scoped). Live image (CE_STACK_LIVE_IMAGE=1) installs Docker CLI +
# .[lightrag-runtime]; CE_DOMAIN_CONTROLLER_IMAGE tags that image for per-domain
# containers. Socket mount is local single-operator only — never production /
# shared multi-tenant. Domain runtimes use internal network ce-domain-runtimes
# with no host-published ports.
#
# Example:
#   export CE_STACK_LIVE_RUNTIME_ROOT=/home/you/.local/share/context-engine/stack-domain-runtimes
#   mkdir -p "$CE_STACK_LIVE_RUNTIME_ROOT"
#   # optional pin (defaults to context-engine-live:local):
#   # export CE_DOMAIN_CONTROLLER_IMAGE=context-engine-live:local
#   docker compose --env-file .env.stack.local \
#     -f compose.stack.yml -f compose.stack.live.yml up --build -d
#
# CE_STACK_LIVE_RUNTIME_ROOT=<absolute host path>
# CE_DOMAIN_CONTROLLER_COMMAND=python -m context_engine.tools.domain_runtime_controller
# CE_DOMAIN_CONTROLLER_IMAGE=context-engine-live:local

# --- Optional MinIO object-store overlay (P10-04 evidence lane; not default CI) ---
# Pins CE_OBJECT_STORE_KIND=s3 via compose.stack.minio.yml. Default compose.stack.yml
# stays filesystem (CE_SOURCE_STORAGE_ROOT volume). MinIO image builds with
# CE_STACK_OBJECT_STORE_IMAGE=1 (boto3 object-store extra).
#
# Credential tiers (do not collapse):
#   MINIO_ROOT_*       — minio + minio-init only
#   CE_S3_*            — api/worker least-privilege (no ListBucket)
#   CE_S3_RECON_*      — operator recon/export scripts only (never mount on api/worker)
#
# Example:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.stack.local \
#     -f compose.stack.yml -f compose.stack.minio.yml up --build -d
#
# MINIO_ROOT_USER=<set locally>
# MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=<set locally — long random>
# CE_S3_BUCKET=ce-objects
# CE_S3_ACCESS_KEY=<set locally — app user>
# CE_S3_SECRET_KEY=<set locally — app secret>
# CE_S3_RECON_ACCESS_KEY=<set locally — recon user>
# CE_S3_RECON_SECRET_KEY=<set locally — recon secret>
# CE_S3_REGION=us-east-1
